      "observed": "The +3V3 net connects the TLV1117 regulator output U20.2 to the FT231XS 3V3OUT output U21.13; U21's VCC pin U21.15 is also on that rail.",
      "expected": "An externally regulated +3V3 rail should not be tied to the FT231XS internal 3V3 regulator output; use the external rail for VCC/VCCIO and leave 3V3OUT isolated as required by the device application guidance.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "+3V3 : ... U20.2(VO,power_out) U21.13(3V3OUT,power_out) U21.15(VCC,power_in) U21.3(VCCIO,power_in)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The external regulator and the FTDI internal regulator output are tied together, potentially causing back-driving or regulator contention and unreliable 3.3 V operation.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C54"],
      "pins": ["C54.1", "C54.2"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "GND"],
      "observed": "C54 is assigned a value of 0.1nF, but its MPN is CC0603KRX7R9BB104, whose 104 code denotes 100nF (0.1uF); its description field also says 0.1uF.",
      "expected": "The value and sourcing metadata should agree. For this +5V-to-GND decoupling position, the listed part metadata indicates 0.1uF, not 0.1nF.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "C54 | 0.1nF 50V | ... Part Description= 0.1uF 10% 16V Ceramic Capacitor ... MPN=CC0603KRX7R9BB104"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "+5V : ... C54.1(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "GND ... C54.2(passive)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The design value and sourced component disagree by a factor of 1000, so the assembled board or a build based on the schematic value may have different decoupling than intended.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The files show a probable e-stop buffer part-number mismatch and an FTDI internal 3.3 V output tied to the external 3.3 V regulator output. C54 also has a clear 1000-fold disagreement between its stated value and sourcing metadata."
}

